[Music]  hey everyone welcome to another  installment of harry potter theory today  we're going to be discussing a topic  that has been bugging me for quite some  time  and that is how on earth did a gigantic  basilisk survive inside of the teeny  tiny chamber of secrets for one thousand  plus years hogwarts is big but not that  big in the chamber though extraordinary  doesn't seem nearly big enough to  accommodate a 50-foot long serpent we're  first introduced to the basilisk which  was the horrific creation of hogwarts  founder salazar sutherin in the chamber  of secrets basilisks are enormous  serpentine creatures the existence of  which can be attributed to their  original twisted creator a dark wizard  by the name of herpo the fowl a common  misconception is that slytherin created  the first basilisk where in reality he  merely created his own the same one that  resides within hogwarts secret chamber  of the many fearsome beasts and monsters  that roam our land there is none more  curious or more deadly than the basilisk  known also as the king of serpents  this snake which may reach gigantic size  and live many hundreds of years is born  from a chicken's egg hatched beneath a  toad its methods of killing are most  wondrous for aside from its deadly and  venomous fangs the basilisk has a  murderous stare  and all who are fixed with the beam of  its eye shall suffer instant death  spiders flee before the basilisk for it  is their mortal enemy and the basilisk  flees only from the crowing of the  rooster which is fatal to it the  basilisk was initially placed inside of  a secret chamber in the school because  salazar disagreed with the other  founders and their philosophy that  muggleborn should be allowed to attend  the school  salazar was a strong advocate of blood  purity and felt that only pure blood  witches and wizards were worthy of  attending the school  unable to influence the way that the  other founders felt salazar created the  basilisk in a last-ditch effort to  effectively rid the school of  muggleborns  knowing that he wouldn't live forever  salazar also put magic in place to  ensure that whoever was his rightful  heir would be able to control the  creature  q voldemort because of this enchantment  any descendant of salazars would be able  to communicate with the giant creature  via parcel tongue the language of snakes  those who are able to speak parcel  tongue are known as parcel mounds and  voldemort was widely known to possess  this ability  as harry potter had a piece of soul  fragment inside of him he also possessed  this ability which is why he was able to  understand the basilisk speaking  however just because harry was a parcel  mouth it did not mean that he was able  to control the basilisk in any capacity  that responsibility was left with the  rightful heir of southern alone tom  riddle when harry first enters the  chamber of secrets he's all struck at  what appears in front of him in stature  and just overall presence the basilisk  of salazar satherin is at this point in  the story the most intimidating  challenge that harry will need to  overcome  okay on to the tricky stuff presumably  salazar created the basilisk either  during the birth of hogwarts or shortly  before departing from hogwarts whichever  way you want to spin it the basilisk was  around a thousand years old when harry  encounters it in the chamber of secrets  which begs the question how on earth did  such an enormous creature  up to 50 feet in length according to  major zoologist newt scamander survive  within the depths of the chamber of  secrets for 1 000 years  don't they eat  according to newt scamander an expert on  the topic a basilisk's lifespan can be  considerable so long as they have a  sufficient food source  the basilisk of herpa default for  example lived to be over 900 years old  he also goes on to add that basilisks  will eat all mammals and birds as well  as most reptiles  the basilisk eating is alluded to in  chapter 16 of the chamber of secrets  when ron steps on a rat's skull  but the tunnel was quiet as the grave  and the first unexpected sound they  heard was a loud crunch as ron stepped  on what turned out to be a rat's skull  harry lowered his wand to look at the  floor and saw that it was littered with  small animal bones  what this passage suggests is that the  basilisk eats a lot of small animals  however i'm certainly not convinced that  a diet of rats would be nearly enough to  sustain such an enormous creature  differences in physiologies aside for a  second i weigh 185 pounds and need to  eat 3 000 calories a day just to  maintain my weight so i can't even begin  to imagine how many calories a herculean  serpent would need  furthermore insatiable hunger and  caloric needs of the basilisk would need  to be met day in and day out for it to  survive stretch that out to 1000 years  and that's going to equate to more than  just a few small animal bones as for a  cannon answer i think that the animal  bones are the best that we're going to  get however i've got a few theories of  my own  theory number one because the basilisk  is actually just a giant snake this is  reinforced in the text in the chamber of  secrets then it would be fairly safe to  assume that the basilisk shares the  typical digestive traits of a snake and  as it turns out snakes are able to lower  their metabolic rates by up to 70  percent which allows them to survive for  prolonged periods without food this  might account for how the basilisk was  able to get by on so very little  but if the basilisk is only eating a  tiny amount of food then how did it end  up growing to such a gargantuan size  well according to various studies on  snakes  their unique genetic predisposition to  continue growing has nothing to do with  nourishment you see according to these  studies snakes will continue to grow  even with a lack of food as they possess  a strong selective advantage which  pushes them to grow longer furthermore  because the basilisk is such a specimen  of a snake magnified in nearly every way  it's not far-fetched to assume that  these metabolic phenomena are amplified  theory number two the basilisk leaves  the chamber we all know that the only  way in and out of the chamber is through  speaking parcel tongue but guess what  parcel tongue the language of snakes is  spoken by the basilisk a snake  what this means is that the basilisk  would have had plenty of opportunities  to head in and out of the chamber over  the millennia that it was trapped inside  it's also suggested at least according  to ron that the chamber of secrets was  actually located under the lake probably  an exact quote  if this is the case then i don't see why  the basilisk would have had any issue  leaving the chamber swimming into the  lake to grab dinner and then swimming  back  avoiding land would also probably  explain why the basilisk went undetected  yes that's right snakes can swim  this theory that the basilisk would come  and go would also explain the location  of the animal bones between the bathroom  pipe entrance and the doors which needed  a password  theory number three the basilisk is  magic therefore trying to apply science  to it is completely nonsensical it  merely survives because it was magically  enchanted to do so  which theory do you guys subscribe to  did you ever wonder how the basilisk  survived within the chamber of secrets  did this question only bother me  leave a comment down below until next  time remember it does not do to dwell on  dreams and forget to live

